.vscode
__pycache__
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints

PD.ipynb
/assests/
# Raw dataset downloads/clones (multi-GB; never committed -- Kaggle mounts these fresh every session)
/data/

# Pipeline output: regenerated every run by scripts/run_data_pipeline.py, and full of
# Kaggle-session-specific absolute paths, so it doesn't belong in git. The small,
# hand/one-time-computed metadata this depends on lives in /data_meta/ instead, which
# IS tracked (see assets/docs/02_taxonomy_mapping.md).
/data_manifests/

# EDA plot output: regenerated every run by src/eda.py, same reasoning as /data_manifests/.
/eda_outputs/

# Training run outputs: checkpoints, per-epoch train/val loss logs, test metrics --
# regenerated every run by scripts/train.py / scripts/run_multi_seed.py, and checkpoints
# alone would blow up repo size. The decisions behind what gets trained live in
# assets/docs/05_modelling_decisions.md / 06_training_guide.md instead, which ARE tracked.
/runs/

# NOTE: assets/docs/*.md (this project's running decision log) is intentionally tracked --
# do not add /assets/ back here. A prior version of this file ignored the whole /assets/
# folder, which silently excluded every doc in assets/docs/ from version control; that was
# a mistake and has been removed.
